k in june but you've gotten into a  tit for tat with several republican  senators ted cruz pat toomey uh who  voted against it this second time around  they're citing a number of reasons break  down what they're saying and what your  message is to them  so it's it's it's kind of complex as  everything is down here because you know  washington dc is like willy wonka  chocolate factory without any chocolate  or candy it's just all these bizarre  rooms that bring no joy to anybody uh  the bill passed uh the house and it went  to the senate they reformed a couple of  things that needed some looking at some  things that would help the va implement  the bill in a more practical way that  wouldn't cause uh any backlogs that  wouldn't cause difficulties with the new  influx of patients and the  specialization of the kind of treatment  they need right so that got done in may  they posted it on congress.gov  that bill which passed out of the  veterans affairs committee in the senate  by unanimous  all republicans all democrats went to  the floor of the senate june 16th it  passed 84 to 14.  so it was ready to go to the president  the house flagged a technical issue in  the bill it's called a blue slip  it had to do with  tax benefits if uh rural providers were  given money by the va to give veterans  who don't have access to the larger  facilities the same type of specialized  care that's all that changed nothing was  added to the bill it's the exact same  bill you can go on congress.gov you can  put them side to side it's the exact  same bill  one sentence removed about taxation for  rural providers  that bill went back oh and by the way it  gained 90 more votes in the house  republicans 90 more republicans then  signed on in the house goes back to the  senate you think it's a rubber stamp  vote  everybody gathers to celebrate  25 republicans in the senate switched  their vote from yes to no when nothing  had changed  so john when you hear when you hear that  um but you you 